import json, pathlib, html, sys
root=pathlib.Path('artifacts/p2loadtest')
s=json.loads(pathlib.Path(sys.argv[1]).read_text())
escape=html.escape
prior=json.loads((root/'middle-summary.json').read_text())
prior_sections={r['km']:r for r in prior['sections']}
rows=''.join('<tr><td>{}</td><td>{}</td><td>{}</td><td>{:.1f}</td><td>{:.1f}</td><td>{:.1f}</td><td>{:.1f}</td></tr>'.format(r['km']+1,r['frames'],f"{prior_sections[r['km']]['updateMs']['p95']:.1f}" if r['km'] in prior_sections else '—',r['updateMs']['p50'],r['updateMs']['p95'],r['updateMs']['p99'],r['renderPreparationMs']['p95']) for r in s['sections'])
route=(root/'route.svg').read_text().replace('width="1200" height="800"','width="100%" height="auto"')
status='Finish crossed and route coverage verified' if s.get('lapCoverageVerified') else 'Finish crossed; inspect coverage' if s['complete'] else 'Incomplete run — not a verified lap'
run_id=sys.argv[2] if len(sys.argv)>2 else '39896651706'
dry=json.loads((root/'dry-catchup.json').read_text())
body=f'''<!doctype html><html lang="en"><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width"><title>P2 endurance test</title><style>
body{{background:#111820;color:#e9eff7;font:17px/1.5 system-ui;max-width:1100px;margin:auto;padding:24px}}h1,h2{{line-height:1.2}}table{{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;display:block;overflow:auto;font-size:14px;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}}td,th{{padding:8px;text-align:right;border-bottom:1px solid #425060}}th{{background:#25313d}}.note{{background:#25313d;padding:16px;border-radius:8px}}svg{{max-height:600px}}li{{margin-bottom:8px}}</style>
<h1>p2loadtest — endurance results</h1><p><strong>{status}</strong> · {s['routeLengthM']/1000:.2f} km route · {s['aiCount']} AI cars plus player · {s['simulatedSeconds']/60:.1f} simulated minutes</p>
<p class="note">This is a Node CPU test of gameplay, physics and road-condition/tire-mark geometry preparation. It does not measure browser drawing, GPU performance, audio or phone FPS. The first five seconds are excluded from the timing table. Driver inputs use the normal vehicle simulation, without teleporting around the route.</p>
{route}<p>Grey: street. Brown: rally. Blue: bridge. Purple: tunnel. P1 skybox, textures and 21.6 m road width are retained.</p>
<h2>CPU time by kilometre</h2><p>The earlier comparison was stopped at 12.26 km after more than an hour. AI car selection varies between runs, so these whole-run comparisons are indicative, not a controlled A/B measurement. The isolated query/weather benchmarks use matching inputs and verify matching outputs.</p><table><thead><tr><th>km</th><th>Frames</th><th>Earlier update p95 ms</th><th>Final update median ms</th><th>Update p95 ms</th><th>Update p99 ms</th><th>Surface/marks p95 ms</th></tr></thead><tbody>{rows}</tbody></table>
<p>Final-run peak sampled process memory (RSS): {s.get('peakRSSMB',0):.0f} MiB. Peak sampled JavaScript heap used: {s.get('peakHeapUsedMB',0):.0f} MiB.</p><p class="note"><strong>This is not yet steady real-time performance with 11 AI.</strong> Update median: {s['cpuMilliseconds']['updateMs']['p50']:.1f} ms; p95: {s['cpuMilliseconds']['updateMs']['p95']:.1f} ms; worst measured update: {s['cpuMilliseconds']['updateMs']['max']:.0f} ms. AI consumed {s.get('aiShareOfUpdatePercent',0):.1f}% of update time. Several AI made little route progress or stopped; the verified full lap is the player's lap, with all eleven AI present, not eleven completed AI laps.</p><h2>Changes and evidence</h2><ul>
<li>Indexed nearest-road queries and cached route costs replace repeated scans and route searches. On P2, 2,000 matching queries took 602.7 ms before and 25.5 ms after on the local test device.</li>
<li>New dry road-condition cells share exact temperature history for matching profiles. Creating 1,000 cells after 60 seconds of clear-weather history took 724.8 ms before and 17.1 ms after, with the same simulation checksum. Wet weather retains the full calculation.</li>
<li>Revisiting 1,000 old dry cells under constant weather took {dry[0]['elapsedMs']:.1f} ms before and {dry[1]['elapsedMs']:.1f} ms after, with matching checksums. Per-step temperature rounding is preserved, including the exact fixed point.</li>
<li>Surface visuals use nearby-cell lookup, cached heights and bounded refresh frequency. Tire-mark retirement updates affected buckets only.</li>
<li>Per-car collision-edge caches now retain 128 recently used areas. A regression test verifies identical wall classification after eviction. The final endurance run includes this cache limit and the constant-weather shortcut.</li>
</ul><p>Progress readings briefly jumped at branch junctions (largest jump: {s['maximumProjectionJumpM']:.1f} m), so coverage was checked separately from the finish flag. All {s['routeCoverage100m']['expected']} 100-metre sections were visited; integrated vehicle speed corresponds to approximately {s['integratedTravelM']/1000:.2f} km of travel.</p><h2>Remaining work to investigate</h2><ul>
<li><strong>AI simulation/contact queries:</strong> {s.get('aiShareOfUpdatePercent',0):.1f}% of update CPU time. Reuse contact/material scratch data, share immutable terrain classification work across cars, and evaluate moving AI simulation off the render thread before reducing physics fidelity.</li>
<li>AI look-ahead creates persistent condition cells; consider transient queries for untouched areas while preserving weather and contamination behavior.</li>
<li><strong>Checkpoint backlog:</strong> only {s['checkpoint']['checkpointCompletedCount']} checkpoints completed; {s['lastProgress']['events']:,} events were retained near the finish. The worst checkpoint service slice was {s['checkpoint']['checkpointMaximumSliceMs']:.1f} ms. Make setup, capture, hashing and commit consistently bounded or move the heavy work off-thread, while preserving worker synchronization and replay.</li>
<li><strong>Surface and tire-mark mesh preparation:</strong> p95 was {s['cpuMilliseconds']['renderPreparationMs']['p95']:.1f} ms. Reuse mesh buffers and update changed patches incrementally; tire-mark bookkeeping alone was a small part of CPU time. GPU drawing remains unmeasured.</li>
<li>Run the same lap in a rendered browser on the target phone to measure actual frame pacing and GPU cost.</li></ul>
<p>Route coverage: {s.get('routeCoverage100m',{}).get('visited','?')} of {s.get('routeCoverage100m',{}).get('expected','?')} 100-metre sections. Peak retained condition cells: {s['peakCells']:,}. Peak tire-mark segments: {s['peakTireMarks']:,}.</p>
<p>Raw summary: <a href="final-summary.json">final-summary.json</a>. Test run: <a href="https://github.com/radiatedsaturn7/chainsaw-aliens/actions/runs/{run_id}">GitHub Actions</a>.</p></html>'''
(root/'report.html').write_text(body)
print(root/'report.html')
